93074765</bdi></a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Witness+to+History%2C+1929%E2%80%931969&amp;rft.place=New+York&amp;rft.pages=159&amp;rft.pub=New+York%2C+Norton&amp;rft.date=1973&amp;rft.isbn=9780393074765&amp;rft.aulast=Bohlen&amp;rft.aufirst=C.E.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.org%2Fdetails%2Fwitnesstohistory00bohl&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AAllies+of+World+War+II" class="Z3988" about="#mwt675" id="mwEXw"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-130" id="cite_note-130" data-mw-footnote-number="128"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEX0"><a href="#cite_ref-130" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEX4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEX8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-130" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt678" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwEYA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite video","href":"./Template:Cite_video"},"params":{"year":{"wt":"1944"},"title":{"wt":"Video: Allies Study Post-War Security Etc. (1944)"},"url":{"wt":"https://archive.org/details/gov.archives.arc.39024"},"publisher":{"wt":"[[Universal Newsreel]]"},"access-date":{"wt":"28 November 2014"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation audio-visual cs1" about="#mwt678" id="mwEYE"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://archive.org/details/gov.archives.arc.39024" class="external text" id="mwEYI"><i id="mwEYM">Video: Allies Study Post-War Security Etc. (1944)</i></a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_Newsreel" title="Universal Newsreel" id="mwEYQ">Universal Newsreel</a>. 1944<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwEYU">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwEYY">28 November</span> 2014</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Video%3A+Allies+Study+Post-War+Security+Etc.+%281944%29&amp;rft.pub=Universal+Newsreel&amp;rft.date=1944&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.org%2Fdetails%2Fgov.archives.arc.39024&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AAllies+of+World+War+II" class="Z3988" about="#mwt678" id="mwEYc"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-UNSC-FIRST-MEETING-131" id="cite_note-UNSC-FIRST-MEETING-131" data-mw-footnote-number="129"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEYg"><a href="#cite_ref-UNSC-FIRST-MEETING_131-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEYk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEYo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-UNSC-FIRST-MEETING-131" class="mw-reference-text reference-text">United Nations Security Council: Official Records: First Year, First Series, First Meeting.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-BBC_Bitesize-1941-132" id="cite_note-BBC_Bitesize-1941-132" data-mw-footnote-number="130"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEYs"><a href="#cite_ref-BBC_Bitesize-1941_132-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEYw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEY0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-BBC_Bitesize-1941-132" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt738" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwEY4" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"The state of the world after World War Two and before the Cold War – The Cold War origins, 1941–1948"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/guides/zt8ncwx/revision/1"},"access-date":{"wt":"4 April 2021"},"publisher":{"wt":"BBC Bitesize"},"language":{"wt":"en-GB"},"quote":{"wt":"The USA entered World War Two against Germany and Japan in 1941, creating the Grand Alliance of the USA, Britain and the USSR. This alliance brought together great powers that had fundamentally different views of the world, but they did co-operate for four years against the Germans and Japanese. The Grand Alliance would ultimately fail and break down into the Cold War."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt738" id="mwEY8"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/guides/zt8ncwx/revision/1" class="external text" id="mwEZA">"The state of the world after World War Two and before the Cold War – The Cold War origins, 1941–1948"</a>. BBC Bitesize<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwEZE">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwEZI">4 April</span> 2021</span>. <q id="mwEZM">The USA entered World War Two against Germany and Japan in 1941, creating the Grand Alliance of the USA, Britain and the USSR. This alliance brought together great powers that had fundamentally different views of the world, but they did co-operate for four years against the Germans and Japanese. The Grand Alliance would ultimately fail and break down into the Cold War.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=The+state+of+the+world+after+World+War+Two+and+before+the+Cold+War+%E2%80%93+The+Cold+War+origins%2C+1941%E2%80%931948&amp;rft.pub=BBC+Bitesize&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.co.uk%2Fbitesize%2Fguides%2Fzt8ncwx%2Frevision%2F1&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AAllies+of+World+War+II" class="Z3988" about="#mwt738" id="mwEZQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Roos-2020-133" id="cite_note-Roos-2020-133" data-mw-footnote-number="131"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEZU"><a href="#cite_ref-Roos-2020_133-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEZY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEZc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Roos-2020-133" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt741" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwEZg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Roos"},"first":{"wt":"Dave"},"date":{"wt":"12 June 2020"},"title":{"wt":"FDR, Churchill and Stalin: Inside Their Uneasy WWII Alliance"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.history.com/news/big-three-allies-wwii-roosevelt-churchill-stalin"},"access-date":{"wt":"4 April 2021"},"website":{"wt":"History.com"},"language":{"wt":"en"},"quote":{"wt":"There were bright hopes that the cooperative spirit of the Grand Alliance would persist after WWII, but with FDR&apos;s death only two months after Yalta, the political dynamics changed dramatically."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRoos2020" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt741">Roos, Dave (12 June 2020). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.history.com/news/big-three-allies-wwii-roosevelt-churchill-stalin" class="external text" id="mwEZk">"FDR, Churchill and Stalin: Inside Their Uneasy WWII Alliance"</a>. <i id="mwEZo">History.com</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwEZs">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwEZw">4 April</span> 2021</span>. <q id="mwEZ0">There were bright hopes that the cooperative spirit of the Grand Alliance would persist after WWII, but with FDR's death only two months after Yalta, the political dynamics changed dramatically.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=History.com&amp;rft.atitle=FDR%2C+Churchill+and+Stalin%3A+Inside+Their+Uneasy+WWII+Alliance&amp;rft.date=2020-06-12&amp;rft.aulast=Roos&amp;rft.aufirst=Dave&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.history.com%2Fnews%2Fbig-three-allies-wwii-roosevelt-churchill-stalin&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AAllies+of+World+War+II" class="Z3988" about="#mwt741" id="mwEZ4"></span></span></li>
